From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE=1: every task/mesh record of vulkan_mesh.bin is built at boot, not only the used list's, and a mesh pipeline made at run time says whether it was on disk; off by default

Task/mesh pipelines were thought never to reach the disk cache: every boot of T88 logs
"Graphics pipeline built on the GPU thread in N ms: mesh, not in the disk cache <hash>", and the
boot's preparation line says "0 task or mesh in vulkan.bin". Neither says that. The runtime report
sets the reason "mesh, not in the disk cache" for every task/mesh pipeline, whether or not
disk_pipelines has its key (CreateGraphicsPipeline, after the kept translation is used); and the
"task or mesh in vulkan.bin" count is the mesh records found in the wrong file, 0 being right.

What run 739 (batch t87-a, T88) shows instead: vulkan_mesh.bin is read at boot (the PS5's RADV
offers VK_EXT_mesh_shader; 256 task and mesh programs are translated on the workers between the
"Total Pipeline Count" line and the preparation), the runtime builds of the walk (23 in 10 s, 21 of
them mesh) are all "made without translating" from kept translations with 0 refused, and the record
count stays at 1876 over the five runs of the batch: nothing is appended again. The same key hashes
(a6a6715e57348ef3, 81b1fd0ba118e6e3) come back at run time in runs 739 and 743, because the used
list keeps a pipeline for two sessions (UsedPipelinesMaxAge) and a walk does not draw every effect
every run. A mesh pipeline made at run time still costs the GPU thread 1-7 ms (kept path) and the
draw then waits for the driver's build of its compute passes (EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE), at the
first draw of foliage or an effect.

With EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE=1 the boot builds every task/mesh record of vulkan_mesh.bin on the
workers, whether or not the used list has it (EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_COLD=1 still builds nothing), and
logs "EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE=1: N task/mesh pipelines of vulkan_mesh.bin built at boot, M of them not
in the used list". The runtime report then says "mesh, not in the disk cache" only for a mesh
pipeline that was not on disk; one that was reads "on disk, not built at boot" or "evicted" like
any other. The file formats, vulkan.bin, vulkan_mesh.bin, vulkan_used.bin and the kept store, are
not touched; unset or anything but "1" changes nothing.

---
 src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 5f97bb0..e69d6a1 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -903,6 +903,20 @@ bool PreloadAllPipelines() {
     }();
     return all;
 }
+
+// EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE=1 (exact "1"): every task/mesh record of vulkan_mesh.bin is built at boot,
+// not only those the used list names. The mesh records are few (run 739: 256 task and mesh
+// programs translated at boot, 10-21 mesh pipelines made during the walk), and a task/mesh
+// pipeline a draw asks for at run time is made on the GPU thread (from its kept translation) and
+// the draw then waits for the driver's build of its compute passes (EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE).
+// Off: the used list decides, as before. EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_COLD=1 wins over it (a cold boot
+// builds nothing). With it, the runtime report tells a mesh pipeline that was on disk ("on disk,
+// not built at boot", "evicted") from one that was not ("mesh, not in the disk cache"); off,
+// every mesh pipeline made at run time is reported as the latter, whether on disk or not.
+bool MeshCacheBoot() {
+    static const bool on = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE");
+    return on;
+}
 } // Anonymous namespace
 
 bool DropMeshDrawsBeforeBuild() {
@@ -1582,6 +1596,8 @@ void PipelineCache::LoadDiskResources(u64 title_id, std::stop_token stop_loading
     std::atomic<size_t> prep_differed{};
     size_t skipped_pipelines = 0;
     size_t queued_graphics = 0;
+    size_t mesh_queued = 0;   // EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE: task/mesh records built at boot ...
+    size_t mesh_unlisted = 0; // ... of them not in the used list (skipped without the switch)
 
     if (use_vulkan_pipeline_cache) {
         vulkan_pipeline_cache_filename = base_dir / "vulkan_pipelines.bin";
@@ -1680,7 +1696,9 @@ void PipelineCache::LoadDiskResources(u64 title_id, std::stop_token stop_loading
 
         const u64 hash = key.Hash();
         disk_pipelines.insert(hash);
-        if (!PreloadAllPipelines() &&
+        // EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE=1: a task/mesh record is built whether or not the used list has it.
+        const bool mesh_always = loading_mesh_file && MeshCacheBoot() && !PipelineColdBoot();
+        if (!PreloadAllPipelines() && !mesh_always &&
             (PipelineColdBoot() ||
              (used_pipelines.empty() ? queued_graphics >= MaxPipelinesWithoutUsedList
                                      : !used_pipelines.contains(hash)))) {
@@ -1688,6 +1706,12 @@ void PipelineCache::LoadDiskResources(u64 title_id, std::stop_token stop_loading
             return;
         }
         ++queued_graphics;
+        if (mesh_always) {
+            ++mesh_queued;
+            if (!used_pipelines.contains(hash)) {
+                ++mesh_unlisted;
+            }
+        }
 
         workers.QueueWork([this, key, envs_ = std::move(envs), &state, &callback, prep,
                            &prep_compared, &prep_differed]() mutable {
@@ -1729,6 +1753,12 @@ void PipelineCache::LoadDiskResources(u64 title_id, std::stop_token stop_loading
                  "{} cached graphics pipelines are built when first needed",
                  skipped_pipelines);
     }
+    if (mesh_queued != 0) {
+        LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                 "EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE=1: {} task/mesh pipelines of vulkan_mesh.bin built at boot, "
+                 "{} of them not in the used list",
+                 mesh_queued, mesh_unlisted);
+    }
     if (UsedListKept()) {
         LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
                  "{}: {} cached graphics pipelines left for their first use, {} built at boot; "
@@ -2303,7 +2333,9 @@ std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline> PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline() {
     // Task and mesh programs are translated with the mesh registers, which vulkan.bin doesn't
     // carry: they go to their own file (builds without it never read those records).
     const bool is_mesh = pipeline->IsMeshPipeline();
-    if (is_mesh) {
+    // EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE=1: "mesh, not in the disk cache" only when it is not; a mesh pipeline
+    // the boot read and left for its first use is reported like any other (off: as before).
+    if (is_mesh && (!MeshCacheBoot() || !disk_pipelines.contains(key_hash))) {
         reason = RuntimeBuild::Mesh;
     }
     if (disk_pipelines.contains(graphics_key.Hash())) {
